#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175684 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176037 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc2759a6-76b0-5410-b695-1e28b3168cb8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution: Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/id #uuid "b26c36dd-e371-5598-96a3-73fb1c147a7c" :question/math-academy-id "e-10048" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n\n$f(x,y) = 5y\\sqrt{x}, \\quad y^2 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\quad y\\geq 0$.\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF $f_Y(y)$." :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y)$, then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\nf_{X}(x) = \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dy, f_{Y}(y) = \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dx\n$$\n\nFirst, let's sketch the region\n\n$$\nD = \\{(x,y) \\::\\: y^2 \\leq x \\leq1,\\, y\\geq 0 \\}\n$$\n\n![](images/4c/4c689a61af43d1d7aef57364a0d231256329305438e3fa046b048b7580fc13fe.png)\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for\n\n$$\n0 \\leq y \\leq 1\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y}(y) &= \\int_{y^{2}}^{1}5y\\sqrt{x}dx \\\\\n&= 5y\\int_{y^{2}}^{1}\\sqrt{x}dx \\\\\n&= 5y[\\frac{2}{3}x^{3/2}]_{x = y^{2}}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{10y}{3}[x^{3/2}]_{x = y^{2}}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{10y}{3}[1^{3/2} - (y^{2})^{3/2}] \\\\\n&= \\frac{10y}{3}[1 - y^{3}] \\\\\n&= (10(y - y^{4}))/(3)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{(10(y - y^{4}))/(3),\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175852 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62a2b5bc-ecf8-5e8e-bf4e-0cde666ec594" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "ed593b5a-be86-5f9a-b9a5-d82b07ed2cfd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9192" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n${\\frac{15}{7}x^{2}y^{4},\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le x \\le 2, 0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF $f_Y(y)$." :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y)$, then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\nf_{X}(x) = \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dy, f_{Y}(y) = \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dx\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for\n\n$$\n0\\leq y \\leq1\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y}(y) &= \\int_{1}^{2}\\frac{15}{7}x^{2}y^{4}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{15}{7}y^{4}[\\frac{1}{3}x^{3}]_{x = 1}^{x = 2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{7}y^{4}[x^{3}]_{x = 1}^{x = 2} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{7}y^{4}(2^{3} - 1^{3}) \\\\\n&= 5y^{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{5y^{4},\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175853 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc918d1c-7446-59a5-ad73-f705f83ae49c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/id #uuid "e0123816-b3f6-5fd4-a6ae-09c31bcce5cd" :question/math-academy-id "e-9193" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n${e^{- (4x + y/4)},\\begin{vmatrix}x \\ge 0, y \\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\nFind $P(-4 \\leq Y \\leq 4)$." :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y)$, then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\nf_{X}(x) = \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dy, f_{Y}(y) = \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dx\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for\n\n$$\ny \\geq 0\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y}(y) &= \\int_{0}^{∞}e^{- (4x + y/4)}dx \\\\\n&= [- \\frac{1}{4}e^{- (4x + y/4)}]_{x = 0}^{x = ∞} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{4}(0 - e^{- (0 + y/4)}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}e^{-y/4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for $f_Y(y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\frac{1}{4}e^{-y/4},\\begin{vmatrix}y \\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required probability is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nP(-4 \\le Y \\le 4) &= \\int_{-4}^{4}f_{Y}(y)dy \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{4}e^{-y/4}dy \\\\\n&= [- e^{-y/4}]_{0}^{4} \\\\\n&= (-e^{-4/4} + e^{0}) \\\\\n&= 1 - \\frac{1}{e}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175854 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176001 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad789c4f-c4e1-5efc-8241-a55e4ac1dd07" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal CDF"}] :question/id #uuid "acab7d19-e027-53cc-b491-58cbd73ee640" :question/math-academy-id "e-9195" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n${\\frac{3}{8}(x + y)^{2},\\begin{vmatrix}-1 \\le x \\le 1,-1 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\n\nFind the marginal cumulative distribution function (CDF) $F_Y(y)$ of $Y$." :question/worked-solution "If $X$ and $Y$ are two continuous random variables with joint probability density function $f(x, y)$, then the marginal density functions for $X$ and $Y$ are\n\n$$\nf_{X}(x) = \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dy, f_{Y}(y) = \\int_{- ∞}^{∞}f(x, y)dx\n$$\n\nIn our case, the marginal density function of $Y$ for\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq y \\leq 1\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_{Y}(y) &= \\int_{-1}^{1}\\frac{3}{8}(x + y)^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{3}{8}[\\frac{1}{3}(x + y)^{3}]_{x =-1}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}[(x + y)^{3}]_{x =-1}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}[(1 + y)^{3} - (-1 + y)^{3}] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}[(y + 1)^{3} - (y - 1)^{3}] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}[(y^{3} + 3y^{2} + 3y + 1) - (y^{3} - 3y^{2} + 3y - 1)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}[(y^{3} + 3y^{2} + 3y + 1) - (y^{3} - 3y^{2} + 3y - 1)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{8}[2(3y^{2} + 1)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}(3y^{2} + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the marginal CDF of $Y$ for\n\n$$\n-1 \\leq y \\leq 1\n$$\n\nis\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF_{Y}(y) &= \\int_{- ∞}^{y}f_{Y}(u)du \\\\\n&= \\int_{-1}^{y}\\frac{1}{4}(3u^{2} + 1)du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}\\int_{-1}^{y}(3u^{2} + 1)du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[u^{3} + u]_{-1}^{y} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[y^{3} + y - (-1)^{3} - (-1)] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{4}[y^{3} + y + 2] \\\\\n&= \\frac{y^{3} + y + 2}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the full expression for the marginal CDF of $Y$ is\n\n$$\n{0,\\begin{vmatrix}y < - 1 \\\\ \\frac{y^{3} + y + 2}{4},\\end{vmatrix}- 1 \\le y \\le 1; 1 \\mid y > 1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175999 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62a2b5bc-ecf8-5e8e-bf4e-0cde666ec594" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a54cef8f-0c6d-5259-bc17-9fb403402f7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = {\\frac{3}{7}y^{2},\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le y \\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173807} {:answer/id #uuid "ab9293e2-b61e-5d0e-8aba-295a9c3ee4fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = {1,\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le y \\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173808} {:answer/id #uuid "b7f114fe-d110-50cd-bc2a-9046dd9a02ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = {\\frac{4}{3}y,\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le y \\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173809} {:answer/id #uuid "3bc2f797-0495-5e6f-bb4c-c45590bf5697" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = {\\frac{2}{3}y,\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le y \\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173810} {:answer/id #uuid "613ab084-957e-5b16-8c8d-1d7a735d6985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = {\\frac{1}{3}y,\\begin{vmatrix}1 \\le y \\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173811}] :answer-field/id #uuid "94e671b2-3bc6-5214-829c-28d39395095c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173806}] :question/id #uuid "299fe748-fc78-5066-b383-fe1227671e5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-110409" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n$f(x, y) = {\\frac{8}{3}x^{3}y,\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, 1 \\le y \\le 2, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF $f_{Y}(y)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176261 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176000 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc918d1c-7446-59a5-ad73-f705f83ae49c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Probability From a Joint Distribution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "855080ee-7d77-5608-a727-98aeca63c799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.896" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173825} {:answer/id #uuid "d5c74169-51d2-5344-a44b-da35014e75ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.104" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173826} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b25d28-14c6-5d5a-b7ed-d5edc59b963e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.658" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173827} {:answer/id #uuid "515d0182-6f19-53ef-9998-81b80b6bb6e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.205" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173828} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7cb9cc-8702-5b2b-b64d-27610d91deb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.342" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173829}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8dd4eda8-fb5d-5a1b-b8c6-e12059aeaa19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173824}] :question/id #uuid "5dd8d5b2-3566-50a9-8091-3b7c245239df" :question/math-academy-id "q-110417" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the joint probability density function\n$f(x, y) = {\\frac{3}{2}(x^{2} + y^{2}),\\begin{vmatrix}0 \\le x \\le 1, 0 \\le y \\le 1, \\\\ 0,\\end{vmatrix}otherwise$.\nFind $P(0.2 < X < 1)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176037 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc2759a6-76b0-5410-b695-1e28b3168cb8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Marginal Distribution From a Joint Distribution: Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e449978b-a0b2-59ff-a42c-46aa92ef386e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = (1)/(π(y^{2} + 1)), - ∞ < y < ∞$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174443} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e82ec9-04de-5d5f-b8d4-bf3aa7f36652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = \\frac{1}{y^{2}}, - ∞ < y < ∞$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174444} {:answer/id #uuid "31a5d3a6-e8e4-55df-a81f-2acb76ebc632" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = (2)/(π(4y^{4} + 1)), - ∞ < y < ∞$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174445} {:answer/id #uuid "38b759f6-a855-5df7-b44f-37eb2f174c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{π}}e^{-y^{2}}, - ∞ < y < ∞$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174446} {:answer/id #uuid "3c730ba8-dad3-5157-874c-030362e0f460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$f_{Y}(y) = e^{-y^{2}}, - ∞ < y < ∞$." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174447}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a96ed7e6-c50b-50a2-b3e6-536e5dec7124" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174442}] :question/id #uuid "19e2e9e5-da57-56e4-b48b-5d2aa326a248" :question/math-academy-id "q-142856" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with a joint probability density function\n\n$f(x, y) = \\frac{1}{πx^{2}}, y^{2} + 1 \\le x$.\n\nFind the expression for the marginal PDF $f_{Y}(y)$."}]}
